    "preview_note": "AMAT's July quarter (reported August 13) was a blowout: record revenue of $9.12B, up 25% y/y and ~$165M above the $8.95B guide midpoint \u2014 the largest sequential dollar growth in company history \u2014 with non-GAAP EPS of $3.50 versus the $3.36 guide. Three things mattered. First, Semiconductor Systems surged to $7.04B (+27% y/y) on DRAM (26% of mix, up from 22%) and leading-edge foundry-logic, validating the HBM/AI capacity thesis. Second, margin quality: 50.4% non-GAAP gross margin marked a 13th straight quarter of y/y expansion, and 34.0% operating margin drove 41% EPS growth. Third, cash: record $3.04B CFO and $2.33B FCF funded $860M of distributions with cash building to $7.1B. The reaction hinges on the Q4 guide \u2014 $10.25B \u00b1 $500M revenue and $4.02 \u00b1 $0.20 EPS implies another ~12% sequential step and ~34% y/y growth, an extraordinary acceleration that de-risks FY26 (~$34.4B) and frames FY27 as 'another strong growth year' per management. Watch China (28% of revenue, down from 35%) and the unrealized strategic-investment loss ($220M) that dragged GAAP EPS to $3.17. Into the November print, the bar is now the guide-plus-beat cadence (~$10.4B/$4.10); DRAM mix and contract-liability growth are the key confirmations that the AI equipment cycle extends into FY27 rather than peaking at the October quarter.",
    "reasoning": "The fiscal Q3 2026 results (quarter ended July 26, 2026) are already in the verified filed record: 8-K accession 0001628280-26-056699, accepted 2026-08-13, before today's 2026-08-20 cutoff. I therefore anchored every income statement, cash flow, and balance sheet line directly on the filed statements: revenue $9,115M, gross profit $4,586M, operating income $3,075M, net income $2,538M on 800M diluted shares ($3.17 GAAP EPS); non-GAAP net income $2,795M (bridge adjustments sum to +$257M, dominated by the $220M unrealized strategic-investment loss add-back); CFO $3,037M, capex -$707M, FCF $2,330M; cash+restricted $7,094M (prior $6,359M + $735M net change); total assets $43,522M = liabilities $17,896M + equity $25,626M. Retained earnings roll-forward per the harness convention: 59,274 + 2,538 - 420 - 440 = 60,952, with other_equity as the -35,326 residual. Guidance_forecast mirrors the actual Q4 FY26 outlook filed in the release ($10.25B \u00b1 $0.5B; $4.02 \u00b1 $0.20). Forward quarters assume AMAT's recent cadence of beating guidance midpoint by ~1.5-2% on revenue and ~$0.08-0.14 on EPS, gross margin ~50.5%, and FY27 revenue of ~$44.7B (+30% y/y, ~9% above the Q4'26 exit run-rate) consistent with management's raised calendar-2026 SSG outlook and explicit expectation of strong 2027 growth; FY28-FY29 moderate toward WFE of $150-155B with widening distributions and cycle-digestion risk reflected in wide p10-p90 bands."
  },
